{"name":"Blackberry","hex":"#43182f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blackberry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fruit-bearing shrub of the aggregate species Rubus fruticosus and some hybrids.","The soft fruit borne by this shrub, formed of a black (when ripe) cluster of drupelets."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To gather or forage for blackberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blackberry","blocks":[{"text":"A blackberry is an edible fruit produced by many species in the genus Rubus in the family Rosaceae, hybrids among these species within the subgenus Rubus, and hybrids between the subgenera Rubus and Idaeobatus. The taxonomy of blackberries has historically been confused because of hybridization and apomixis so that species have often been grouped together and called species aggregates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Ripe%2C_ripening%2C_and_green_blackberries.jpg/330px-Ripe%2C_ripening%2C_and_green_blackberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackberry","wikidata":"Q19842373"},{"title":"BlackBerry","blocks":[{"text":"BlackBerry (BB) is a discontinued brand of mobile devices and related mobile services, originally developed and maintained by the Canadian company Research In Motion until 2016. The first BlackBerry was a two-way pager, Inter@ctive Pager 950, launched in 1999 in North America, running on the Mobitex network and became very popular because of its \"always on\" state and ability to send and receive email messages wirelessly. The BlackBerry pioneered push notifications and popularized the mobile QWERTY keyboard, which became a trademark feature of the brand."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/BlackBerry_Bold9700.jpg/330px-BlackBerry_Bold9700.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BlackBerry","wikidata":"Q171819"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/500px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/1280px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/500px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg/250px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg/500px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg/250px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalved_blackberry_(Rubus_fruticosus).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/250px-Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/330px-Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o